{"title":"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Observe that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/f/dcf8af785fd4feed6700c123d56d09de8ce6939a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 2^2+3^2+6^2 &amp;= 7^2 \\\\ 3^2+4^2+12^2 &amp;= 13^2 \\\\ 4^2+5^2+20^2 &amp;= 21^2 \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"151\" height=\"72\" />\n</p><p>(a) Find integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/7/7b7faa33f9c3985c1152e40a327c6d0a1210ed32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^2+6^2+x^2=y^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(b) Conjecture a general rule that is being illustrated here.\n</p><p>(c) Prove your conjecture.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(a) We can rewrite the given equation as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63cdf60ccae4a472305cb1a10676e8285d30c12a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2-x^2 = 25+36 = 61$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"184\" height=\"20\" />. Use difference of squares to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa9c8fab74c4b6d9519a01bd2f9474343e247944.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(y + x)(y - x) = 61$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"20\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/866b44935f69a5b800547127fe13210bb1e36fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$61$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> is a prime we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fd51e2c6c540d944cae07a864960fccb62214b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(y + x) = 61 \\text{ and } (y - x) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"228\" height=\"20\" />, giving us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/2/31254b1e31d04ca0de0314529a003e6c70fb291d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 30 \\text{ and } y = 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n(b) It is not too hard to notice that the LHS above is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/7/587e581b61369ffe551fdf3881e3cce4818043a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 + (n+1)^2 + (n(n+1))^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"217\" height=\"21\" /> and the RHS above is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/1/561384dac996549378784d49c99a3dd08f97027a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n(n+1)+1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"21\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/d/97d5a348205bd16cd565040c9a797d592117c59a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2, 3, 4 \\text{ and } 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"17\" />. We will prove that the LHS <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5eb8726a34932d28103ce7ce17456421222603f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"9\" /> RHS for all integers (although the proof extends to real numbers) in (c).\n</p><p><br />\n(c) We expand the LHS to obtain \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb1d77cb84215abc85cf08a7daf2dcea5055ab4d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} n^2 + n^2 + 2n + 1 + n^2(n^2 + 2n + 1) &amp;= n^4 + 2n^3 + 3n^2 + 2n + 1 \\\\ &amp;= (n^4 + n^3 + n^2) + (n^3 + n^2 + n) + (n^2 + n + 1) \\\\ &amp;= (n^2 + n + 1)^2 \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"662\" height=\"75\" /> \nThus LHS = RHS and we are done.\n~AK2006\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II\" title=\"1993 UNCO Math Contest II\">1993 UNCO Math Contest II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems\" title=\"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://uncmathcontest.wordpress.com/\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1993 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_Northern_Colorado_Math_Contest\" title=\"University of Northern Colorado Math Contest\"> All UNCO Math Contest Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017184130\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.021 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.039 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 128/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1407/2097152 bytes\nTemp